{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439928-best-renown-to-splash","id":439928,"title":"Best renown to 'splash'?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T08:16:08-07:00","id":439928,"title":"Best renown to 'splash'?","content":"Just wondering if anyone is particularly enamored with certain facets, to the point that they would bend over backwards to make sure they have them at chargen or aim to get a point of said renown asap?<br /> <br /> Just as an example (no book on hand) Being a Storm Lord means you have access to Weather and a point of Honor no matter what. The Honor Weather facet, Hunt Under Iron Skies? I think that is so awesomely, essentially Imnir that I would want it no matter what, ...but let's say I loved the Purity facet of weather instead... Yet wasn't playing a Rahu - good thing that third dot of renown is available for wherever you want it, eh?<br /> <br /> So! Any facet you like so much you wish you could get it twice? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:42:37-07:00","id":439969,"title":"","content":"too much!<br /> I actually love Fog of War, Hit and Run, Grasp of howling Wind. Lay low the challenger and Hunt of Fire and Ice ... And also a lot of insight gifts!<br /> I builded my new storm lords rahu (10xp) trying to get some of those gits but I have to wait for hunt of fire and ice and hit and run , arg.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:56:22-07:00","id":439983,"title":"","content":"I don't know about it being essential, but Command Artifice looks like it could do a lot for you. Or you could just run for <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ex_Machina_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">mayor</a>.<br /> <br /> There were a lot of gifts I wanted a lot. The Weather gifts and some of the elemental things. I thought I'd be more interested in the Wisdom facets. But when designing my character I was able to stick close to character concept without having to look outside gifts available. It didn't stop me from making a list of gifts to get after play has started, though. I think Skin Thief is first on the list, the Wolf Gift I went for was Gaze of the Moon.<br /> <br /> Glory, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-14-2015, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T09:32:16-07:00","id":440010,"title":"","content":"I want to make an Irraka Hunter in Darkness with my third starting Renown dot in Honor just so I can begin play with Maze Ward (Warding, Cunning) to protect unwitting travelers from wandering into my <i>mus-rah</i> and Knotted Paths (Nature, Honor) so those unlucky enough to find their way into it won't be able to get out again before I've satisfied my oath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:24:43-07:00","id":440112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439928-best-renown-to-splash?p=440010#post440010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to make an Irraka Hunter in Darkness with my third starting Renown dot in Honor just so I can begin play with Maze Ward (Warding, Cunning).</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that those two facet renowns aren't switched still really irks me. Seems like the Honor renown has more cunning uses, and the reverse is true for the Cunning renown facet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:54:50-07:00","id":440144,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you want to be playin'.<br /> <br /> If I want to be a Social powerhouse<i> at all</i>, I splash Cunning. Because Primal Allure (Dominance) + Prey on Weakness (Insight) basically mean that the Social Maneuvering system is basically mine to play around with.<br /> <br /> A starting Storm Lord Irraka makes a <i>damn</i> scary social character; grab Primal Allure (Cunning, Dominance) and Deny Everything (Honor, Evasion), and <i>rock out</i>. I'd drop your last dot of Renown on either Honor (to boost Deny Everything) or Purity (so you can pick up Snarl of the Predator (Purity, Dominance) ASAP, as well as getting Unity (Purity, Inspiration) at some point). If you're using Charlaquin's character creation houserule, go with the dot of Purity to grab Snarl of the Predator.<br /> <br /> There's <i>nothing</i> quite like convincing people to do stuff for you <i>in combat time</i>.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if I want to be the big bad fightan' Wolf, I go with Glory, because Berserker's Might is pretty great.<br /> <br /> The real takeaway, though, is that Primal Allure is <i>so damn good</i> if you want to do anything with the Social Maneuvering system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:11:15-07:00","id":440709,"title":"","content":"Purity. Fathers form gift. My cahalith blood Talon needs to express the lore to the lodge of the einherjar in the true form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:16:49-07:00","id":440892,"title":"","content":"Honor seems to be the MVP. It has the largest number of Facets that absolutely rock.<br /> But it also has the most roleplaying baggage, so it balances out to a certain degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T01:55:24-07:00","id":441109,"title":"","content":"Imo, Purity. It gives a nice mix of combat and utility independent of one's Purity rank.<br /> <br /> If you are Rahu and thus maxing out Purity asap, then any of the other ones will do depending on what other set of skills you want to tack on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T12:09:30-07:00","id":441686,"title":"","content":"Between the Facets for Death, Insight, Knowledge, Nature, and Strength, I'd say Glory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T07:40:14-07:00","id":444178,"title":"","content":"Each Renown has its particular strengths in terms of the brand of Facets it has access to; I'm not sure I could pin down a favourite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}